WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.470
Creator Robert Kirkman is finally ready to
talk about what caused the fictional zombie

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.450
pandemic in The Walking Dead.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:11.120
For fans who have been following the story
of The Walking Dead since Rick Grimes first

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.990
awoke from his coma back in 2003, this revelation
is a long time coming.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.890
It's actually impressive that Kirkman has
kept his cards so close to his vest for so

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:25.330
long considering the franchise has expanded
to infect every quadrant of our media world:

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.880
video games, books, TV you name it.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:33.290
Now, having reached the epic conclusion of
his long-running tale, at least in comic form,

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.150
Kirkman must have decided it was finally time
to dole out a little fan service.

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:42.140
Early on in the comic series, it's revealed
that every human in the world is already infected

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:47.290
with the zombie pathogen; while zombie bites
accelerate the transformation, any death eventually

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:48.600
results in zombification.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:54.030
We've seen survivors navigate every facet
of this deadly scenario without any understanding

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.760
of the zombie horde's origins.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.070
Well, wonder no more.

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:03.360
On Twitter, Kirkman finally confirmed that
the cause of this pandemic is extraterrestrial

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.059
in nature.

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:06.520
"Aliens."

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:12.909
Specifically, the zombie virus came from a
"space spore," in Kirkman's own words.

00:01:12.909 --> 00:01:17.020
Kirkman has long credited the work of the
late horror movie director George A. Romero

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.350
as a key inspiration for The Walking Dead.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:24.140
He's said on numerous occasions that his entire
magnum opus resulted from the question, "What

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.770
if a zombie movie just kept going?"

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:32.619
In light of this, the space spore explanation
may be yet another homage to Romero particularly

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:37.819
his iconic zombie flick Night of the Living
Dead, wherein the zombie apocalypse has potentially

00:01:37.819 --> 00:01:42.090
been instigated by radiation released from
a space probe to Venus.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:47.389
"That's the space vehicle which orbited Venus
and then was purposefully destroyed by NASA

00:01:47.389 --> 00:01:51.759
when scientists discovered it was carrying
a mysterious high-level radiation."

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:55.520
Fans weren't sure they'd ever get a straight
answer from Kirkman as to what started the

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.409
zombie virus in The Walking Dead.

00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:02.000
In a 2018 Q&amp;A on Tumblr, he dismissed the
notion of revealing the source of the zombie

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.720
contagion as irrelevant to the story, saying:

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.150
"Maybe years after it's all over I'll just
casually mention it in an interview.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.610
That seems like a very J.K.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.000
Rowling thing to do."

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.420
Shots fired!

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.770
Fortunately for curious fans, it seems like
Kirkman found his inner Rowling.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:22.060
On the surface, it may not seem like Kirkman's
earthbound tale of humans surviving against

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:27.180
impossible odds has much to do with extraterrestrials,
but the alien explanation has always been

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.410
bubbling around the edges of The Walking Dead.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:33.940
When Kirkman and his creative team originally
pitched the idea to Image Comics, Kirkman

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:38.920
had to concoct an outlandish backstory for
the series just to catch executives' attention.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.390
At that time, he told a substantial white
lie that the zombie pandemic in The Walking

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.720
Dead was designed by aliens who intended to
use the zombie apocalypse to make Earth a

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.580
softer target for invasion.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:53.870
Although Kirkman was pretty clear that this
was never really his team's intention, it

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:57.150
wasn't the last mention of E.T.'s in The Walking
Dead history.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:03.030
While not necessarily canon, a bonus ending
for issue #75 was inspired by this misleading

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.030
pitch.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:09.560
In this sci-fi re-skin, a lightsaber-wielding
Michonne explains that hostile aliens unleashed

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:14.590
the zombie horde to turn humanity into a race
of slaves bound into service by harvesting

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.540
water, which their alien overlords use as
currency.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.180
How's that for an alternate ending?

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:24.370
Aside from the explanation of the virus being
"totally irrelevant" to the comic series,

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:28.570
Kirkman also believes that the TV iterations
of his work are unlikely to explore either

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.530
the source of or cure for the virus.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:35.791
While certain fans may prefer a pat resolution
to the apocalypse plaguing the world of The

00:03:35.791 --> 00:03:38.820
Walking Dead, Kirkman's instincts are probably
spot-on.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:44.280
The third TV series for the franchise, The
Walking Dead: World Beyond, takes place a

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:49.350
decade after the beginning of the zombie pandemic,
with a set of young protagonists still grappling

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.860
with the world of the undead.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:55.540
"The end of the world was our beginning."

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:59.870
The lack of a cure is definitely organic to
Kirkman's original vision.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:04.340
The Walking Dead has never been a series about
finding a miraculous cure it's a story about

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:09.230
survivors re-establishing a new normal in
a world that will never be the same.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.770
Discovering a cure would undermine the entire
premise.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:16.280
But hey, at least we officially know what
started the collapse in the first place.

